data: {"choices":[{"delta":{"reasoning_content":"Now I need to write a dispatch file for the developer. I should include all the requirements. The developer's own brief is in the input files, but they may not see it automatically - I need to give them what they need. Actually, the developer has their own brief in their clone? No - the developer only sees what I send them. So I should include the key instructions from the developer brief and the full DESIGN.md.\n\nLet me write a comprehensive dispatch file."},"finish_reason":null,"index":0,"raw_output":null}],"created":1789849027,"id":"chatcmpl-11e020dab4e0416fa8a72b99f7a701f5","model":"accounts/fireworks/models/kimi-k2p7-code","object":"chat.completion.chunk","usage":null}

data: {"choices":[{"delta":{"tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"content\": \"# Developer dispatch: implement the Hello greeting app\\n\\n## Your task\\n\\nImplement the design in `DESIGN.md` (already pushed into your clone at `refs/campaign/orchestrator`). Commit the complete React + Vite application to your branch and reply.\\n\\n## Getting the design\\n\\nRun these commands in your repository:\\n\\n```sh\\ngit merge refs/campaign/orchestrator\\n```\\n\\nThen read `DESIGN.md` at the repository root.\\n\\nIf `refs/campaign/orchestrator` is missing, stop and report it immediately.\\n\\n## Technical stack\\n\\n- React with Vite.\\n- Hold the active colour in `useState`.\\n- Install `@codesweep-ai/ui` with `npm install @codesweep-ai/ui` (let npm write the version range into `package.json`; do not write the word `latest` yourself).\\n- The package has optional peer dependencies (`mermaid`, `puppeteer`, `pixelmatch`, `pngjs`). This app needs none of them, so leave them out.\\n\\n## Required design-system usage\\n\\n- Wrap the page in `AppShell` from `@codesweep-ai/ui`. Place `Header` and `Footer` inside it (these are exported by the `AppShell` module).\\n- Use the `Button` component from `@codesweep-ai/ui` for the four colour-change buttons.\\n- Apply these exact CSS custom-property tokens to the greeting colour:\\n  - `--color-cat-2` (teal) — default on load\\n  - `--color-cat-3` (amber)\\n  - `--color-cat-4` (rose)\\n  - `--color-cat-9` (sky)\\n- Import the design-system styles once at the entry point:\\n\\n```js\\nimport \\\"@codesweep-ai/ui/styles/core.css\\\";\\nimport \\\"@codesweep-ai/ui/styles/components/app-shell.css\\\";\\nimport \\\"@codesweep-ai/ui/styles/components/button.css\\\";\\n```\\n\\n## Content\\n\\n- Header title (left side, in the sticky dark header): `Hello`\\n- Footer (dark bar at the bottom): `Built with @codesweep-ai/ui`\\n- Main greeting: `Hello, world!`\\n- Four buttons, left to right, labelled: `Teal`, `Amber`, `Rose`, `Sky`\\n- Clicking a button changes the greeting colour to that button's token.\\n\\n## Layout\\n\\n- Main content sits between the Header and Footer, fills the remaining viewport, and centers the greeting and buttons both vertically and horizontally.\\n- Buttons are in a single horizontal row with equal spacing.\\n\\n## Files to create and commit\\n\\n- `.gitignore`: `node_modules/` and `dist/`\\n- `package.json`: React + Vite dependencies, `@codesweep-ai/ui` dependency, build/serve scripts\\n- `vite.config.js`: bind dev server to `0.0.0.0:5173`\\n- `index.html`\\n- `src/main.jsx` (or `.tsx`) with the style imports above\\n- `src/App.jsx` (or `.tsx`) implementing the design\\n- `README.md` at the root naming the build command and the serve command\\n\\n## Reply\\n\\nReport:\\n1. The branch you committed to.\\n2. The build command from `README.md`.\\n3. The serve command from `README.md`.\\n4. Whether the app matches every requirement in `DESIGN.md`.\\n\", \"filePath\": \"/tmp/dispatch-developer.md\"}","name":"write"},"id":"write_29","index":0,"type":"function"}]},"finish_reason":null,"index":0,"raw_output":null}],"created":1789849027,"id":"chatcmpl-11e020dab4e0416fa8a72b99f7a701f5","model":"accounts/fireworks/models/kimi-k2p7-code","object":"chat.completion.chunk","usage":null}

